-- title:
--   Schlessinger's criterion in one variable: R ≅ Λ[[X]]
-- statement:
--   Let $\Lambda$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring that is adically complete with respect to its maximal ideal, and let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian local $\Lambda$-algebra, likewise adically complete for its maximal ideal, such that the composite $\Lambda \to R \to R/\mathfrak m_R$ of the structure map with the residue map is surjective. Assume the following formal smoothness hypothesis: for all commutative Artinian local $\Lambda$-algebras $A$ and $B$ (in the universe of $\Lambda$) for which $\Lambda \to A \to A/\mathfrak m_A$ and $\Lambda \to B \to B/\mathfrak m_B$ are surjective, every surjective $\Lambda$-algebra map $\pi \colon B \to A$ whose kernel is annihilated by $\mathfrak m_B$ (that is, $xy = 0$ for all $x \in \ker \pi$ and $y \in \mathfrak m_B$), and every $\Lambda$-algebra map $g \colon R \to A$, admits a $\Lambda$-algebra map $g' \colon R \to B$ with $g'$ followed by $\pi$ equal to $g$. Assume further that $t \in \mathfrak m_R$ satisfies $\mathfrak m_R \subseteq (t) + \mathfrak m_R^2 + \mathfrak m_\Lambda R$ and $t \notin \mathfrak m_R^2 + \mathfrak m_\Lambda R$, where $\mathfrak m_\Lambda R$ denotes the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_\Lambda$. Then there exists an isomorphism of $\Lambda$-algebras $e \colon \Lambda[[X]] \xrightarrow{\sim} R$ with $e(X) = t$.
--
--   This is the one-variable case of Schlessinger's criterion: a complete Noetherian local $\Lambda$-algebra whose functor of points on Artinian local $\Lambda$-algebras is formally smooth and whose relative cotangent space $\mathfrak m_R/(\mathfrak m_R^2 + \mathfrak m_\Lambda R)$ is spanned by a single element $t$ is the power series ring $\Lambda[[X]]$, with $X \mapsto t$. It is used to identify unobstructed deformation rings with one-dimensional tangent space, and feeds the variant [`IsLocalRing.exists_powerSeries_algEquiv_of_forall_exists_comp_eq_of_forall_algHom_dualNumber`](thm.html#IsLocalRing.exists_powerSeries_algEquiv_of_forall_exists_comp_eq_of_forall_algHom_dualNumber), in which the cotangent condition is replaced by a condition on $\Lambda$-algebra maps to the dual numbers; the surjection $\Lambda[[X]] \to R$ comes from [`IsLocalRing.exists_mvPowerSeries_algHom_apply_X_eq_and_surjective_of_span`](thm.html#IsLocalRing.exists_mvPowerSeries_algHom_apply_X_eq_and_surjective_of_span) via [`MvPowerSeries.exists_algEquiv_powerSeries_fin_succ`](thm.html#MvPowerSeries.exists_algEquiv_powerSeries_fin_succ).
